"Design a better way to update assets that avoids a complete replacement (admin_apply_bundle currently clears every asset table and reinserts). User's design: make string names truly canonical for the bundle operation. On push, replace the contents of a pre-existing asset that has the same name, in place. Propagate index changes based on these names, so entities holding old indices remap to the new ones. If a name is not unique within its asset array, fail early -- even have the client emit the error, and in dev mode crash the backend. Key rationale: the backend uses indices as cheap identifiers for high-frequency asset lookup, whereas the one-off bundle operation can safely treat names as canonical instead. Supersedes admin_apply_bundle's clear-and-reinsert and its 'store old contents / remap indexes' TODO."